course: dictionary
lesson: 16142
title: Wilful and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A wilful person is stubborn. They have decided what they want, and they keep doing it even when someone tells them to stop. «The wilful princess refused to eat her supper, however much her mum begged.» The word «refused» is a clue: she will not do what she is asked, so wilful must mean stubborn.
explain: Wilful can also describe something done on purpose, especially something bad. «The man was fined for wilful damage to the bus shelter.» Damage is harm, and the word wilful tells you the harm was not an accident. Ask yourself: did they mean to do it? If yes, wilful fits.
explain: The word has a close partner, wilfully, which describes how someone does something: «She wilfully ignored the sign.» It means she did it on purpose, knowing better. Wilfulness is the noun, the quality of being wilful. Remember that in UK English the spelling is wilful, while in US English it is willful.
fact: Wilful means stubborn and determined to do what you want, even when told not to.
fact: Wilful can also mean done on purpose, especially something bad, such as «wilful damage».
fact: «Wilfully» means in a wilful way, on purpose.
fact: «Wilfulness» is the quality of being wilful.
fact: Wilful is spelled with one l in UK English and «willful» with two l in US English; both mean the same thing.
exercise: «The wilful princess refused to eat her supper, however much her mum begged.» What does wilful mean here? | Very kind and gentle | *Stubborn, set on doing what she wants | Hungry and tired | Lost in the castle
exercise: The court said the damage to the bus shelter was wilful. What does wilful damage mean? | Harm done by accident | Harm caused by the weather | Harm that nobody can see | *Harm done on purpose
exercise: A child stamps her foot and shouts, «I won't do it, and you can't make me!» Which word fits her best? | *Wilful | Hungry | Sleepy | Shy
test: «The wilful goat would not come down from the wall, however much the farmer called.» What does wilful mean in this sentence? | Hungry for grass | *Stubborn and determined to do as it wants | Very quiet and calm | Frightened of heights
test: Which word means the same as wilful in «She is headstrong and will not listen to anyone»? | Shy | *Headstrong | Gentle | Sleepy
exam: Which spelling is used in UK English for this word? | wilfull | willful | *wilful | wilfal
